	quest.27A11A6ED27A72D2.quest_desc: [
		"Transformers can raise or lower the &3voltage&r based on the ratio of wire turns on each of their &6electromagnetic coils.&r For example, an input coil of &a100 turns&r and an output of &a400 turns&r would result in a turn ratio of &e4,&r which would boost the voltage by 4X."
		""
		"Coils are added by right clicking them on the transformer. The &binput coil&r is always placed first followed by the &6output&r (or in real life terms, &3primary&r and &6secondary&r coils)."
		""
		"Currently, the transformer doesn't have a good way to tell the input from output except for the noise texture on top. They are not bidirectional. The top part of the \"handle\" with the checkerboard &0🙿&r looking pattern is the &binput&r side. It will be on the left side when you place the block."
	]
	quest.27A11A6ED27A72D2.quest_subtitle: "This is why Westinghouse won."
