	quest.5B7E5A2F7F5C9A1D.quest_desc: [
		"The foundation of waystones teleportation begins with Warp Dust."
		""
		"Mix together AE2 Ender Dust, Fluix Dust, and Create's Powdered Obsidian with water in a Mixing Basin. This requires superheating the mixture to complete the magical transformation."
	]
	quest.5B7E5A2F7F5C9A1D.title: "Magical Dust"
	quest.5B94ED55FD15C110.quest_desc: ["§7To create §fPowdered Obsidian§7, you'll need to process obsidian blocks through a §fCrushing Wheel§7."]
	quest.5B94ED55FD15C110.title: "Obsidian -> Powdered Obsidian"
	quest.5B9501552E5DFB20.quest_desc: ["Found in veins near the surface alongside crimsite and sand."]
	quest.5B9501552E5DFB20.quest_subtitle: "It's clay but... red?"
	quest.5B960A074B904E80.quest_desc: [
		"The &2electrical motor&r converts electrical power into SU, with a small efficiency loss."
		""
		"This is a multi-step deploying recipe, with one step involving the &ewinding machine&r."
		"Start with a &6shaft&r and do the following steps:"
		""
		"1. Use a &ewinding machine&r to wrap 75 turns of &6copper wire&r around it"
		"2. Magnet"
		"3. Steel mechanism"
		"4. Screwdriver"
		""
		"Repeat this three times for a 94% chance of getting a motor."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Rotation direction can be configured."
		""
		"&30V - 320V&r"
		"SU output and speed of the motor depends on the input voltage, up to &611,220SU at 255RPM&r. This consumes &c960W&r of power."
		""
		"&3320V - 1000V&r"
		"Still produces its maximum SU but consumes more power. No point going here."
	]
	quest.5B960A074B904E80.quest_subtitle: "Rotation on demand."
	quest.5B960A074B904E80.title: "Electric Motor"
	quest.5B98CCFA73B83F21.quest_desc: [
		"Create automation for your interplanetary resource gathering operations."
		""
		"Use Create mechanisms and Ad Astra technology to build self-sustaining systems that can gather, process, and transport resources across the solar system."
		""
		"§7Automated systems are essential for efficient large-scale operations across multiple planets."
	]
	quest.5B98CCFA73B83F21.title: "Automated Space Industry"
	quest.5B9A3C87B25AF76C.quest_desc: [
		"Andesite Alloy is your first step into the world of Create!"
		"You'll need this material to craft many basic mechanical components."
		""
		"§7Tip: Create mod uses andesite alloy as a base material for many early-game machines."
		""
		"§7Tip: Make extra - you'll need quite a bit of this alloy later."
	]
	quest.5B9A3C87B25AF76C.title: "Your First Alloy"
	quest.5BB277488E00409F.quest_desc: [
		"Add some comfort to your home with proper furniture!"
		"A chair and table make a dining area feel complete."
		""
		"§7Tip: Place carpets under furniture for a cozy feel."
		""
		"§7Tip: Different wood types create different furniture styles!"
	]
	quest.5BB277488E00409F.title: "Furnishing Fundamentals"
	quest.5BD78F2FCDC8D41A.quest_desc: [
		"§7Dive into the world of §fDumplings Delight§7, where steamed perfection awaits!"
		""
		"§7Automating dumpling production requires precise coordination of ingredients and machinery."
		""
		"§fSetup:§7"
		"§71. Automate §fflour production§7 for dumpling wrappers using §fslicers§7"
		"§72. Set up §fmixers§7 to combine flour and water for the dough"
		"§73. Prepare fillings using §fcutting boards§7 and §fslicers§7"
		"§74. Use §fdeployers§7 to fold dumplings and §fcooking pots§7 to steam them"
		""
		"§fTIP:§7 Different fillings yield different effects! Experiment with combinations for optimal results."
	]
	quest.5BD78F2FCDC8D41A.title: "Steamed Dumpling Automation"
	quest.5BE1B13E934BBA98.quest_subtitle: "Used as well as tank upgrade to move liquids"
	quest.5C06543962E420C4.quest_subtitle: "A motor that converts energy(E) into kinetic energy(SU) at any rpm."
	quest.5C0ECADAA9C5E062.quest_desc: [
		"Lost underground many years ago, these heavily armored knights are not men nor are they statues. Are they guarding something? They have forgotten what. Are they waiting for something? They have forgotten when. Are they mourning someone? They have forgotten whom. All they know is to slay those who approach their chambers. There is only one way to damage a Ferrous Wroughtnaut; its weakness is for you to discover."
		""
		"Only the bravest of adventurers would dare to challenge a Ferrous Wroughtnaut. Upon defeat, the Wroughtnaut will drop its Wrought Helm and its Axe of a Thousand Metals for the victor. Right clicking with the axe attacks in a large arc, and shift-right clicking will create a shockwave that brings targets closer to you. Neither tool can break."
	]
	quest.5C1E3564EC1DA17A.title: "Obtain a &6Silence Armour Trim&r"
	quest.5C21D02BB2644A39.quest_desc: [
		"Despite what the tooltip says, it still takes in &6magnetic alloy&r."
		""
		"Connect it to a generator, place one alloy on the prongs, and watch the needle go up until &eZAP!&r You get a magnet."
	]
	quest.5C21D02BB2644A39.quest_subtitle: "Grug make magnets in civilized manner."
	quest.5C251AB7110F0E5F.quest_subtitle: "Huge Diesel Engines connect to Shafts, they will start generating Kinetic Energy, once you give them some fuel."
	quest.5C3180BD9AD7E0C9.quest_desc: [
		"If you've completed Chapter 3: Industrial Revolution, you already have basic train components."
		""
		"This chapter builds on that foundation and explores:"
		"§71. Advanced train decorations and aesthetics"
		"§72. Create Railways Navigator functionality"
		"§73. Steam 'n' Rails addon features"
		"§74. Train control and management systems"
		""
		"§7Use your existing trains as a starting point for more complex and beautiful railway networks!"
	]
	quest.5C3180BD9AD7E0C9.title: "Beyond Basic Trains"
	quest.5C4BC3F01DD67AD6.quest_desc: [
		"§6Neon District Design"
		""
		"Create a vibrant, night-time cityscape!"
		""
		"§7Design elements to include:"
		"§7• Colored lamps and light sources"
		"§7• Neon signs using colored blocks"
		"§7• Dark backgrounds to make lights pop"
		"§7• Urban details like vents and pipes"
		""
		"§6Pro Tip: §7Use redstone lamps behind stained glass for glow effects"
	]
	quest.5C4BC3F01DD67AD6.title: "§eNeon Designer"
	quest.5C5DE3ECE4E39C5F.quest_subtitle: "Trigger an Overstress Clutch"
	quest.5C5DE3ECE4E39C5F.title: "Circuit Breaker"
	quest.5C726D0A9F70EC89.title: "Obtain a &2Wayfinder Armour Trim&r"
	quest.5C83BEB7E99A0546.quest_desc: [
		"§6Legacy Blocks Collection"
		""
		"Blockus includes several other nostalgic items from Minecraft's past!"
		""
		"§7Other legacy items include:"
		"§7• Crying Obsidian (pre-official version)"
		"§7• Legacy stonecutters"
		"§7• Beta-era block textures"
		"§7• Other retro decorations"
		""
		"§6Pro Tip: §7Create a Minecraft museum showcasing the evolution of the game"
	]
	quest.5C83BEB7E99A0546.title: "§eLegacy Blocks Collection"
	quest.5CDDAD4D40B67D7B.quest_subtitle: "A redstone component that extends a pulse to a configurable amount."
	quest.5CE78B938070D81B.title: "Bake your first Kruidnoten"
	quest.5CF2DDE21ABD5926.quest_desc: [
		"§7This branch provides §fideas and inspiration§7 for creative ComputerCraft projects!"
		""
		"§7These quests don't require crafting specific items - they're guides to help you explore the full potential of your computers."
		""
		"§7Follow these project ideas to create useful tools, entertaining systems, and powerful automation for your world."
	]
	quest.5CF2DDE21ABD5926.title: "ComputerCraft Projects"
	quest.5D0986618729A519.quest_subtitle: "A block that can look for specific items in the world or in inventories."
	quest.5D0986618729A519.title: "I'm watching you."
	quest.5D0C663AAC09A86D.quest_desc: [
		"§7Using a §fDeployer §7holding planks, deploy it onto a shaft to create a cogwheel."
		""
		"§7Tip: Have two paralell production lines for this, since you will need it for both the large cogwheels and for the andesite mechanism"
	]
	quest.5D0C663AAC09A86D.title: "Planks + Shafts -> Cogwheel"
	quest.5D114E6833D0AAF3.quest_desc: [
		"§7Combine §fTuff§7, §fGlowstone Dust§7, §fWater§7, and §fMoon Cobblestone§7 in a §fMixer§7."
		""
		"§7This process yields 2 Moon Cobblestone, creating an efficient production loop."
		""
		"§7Set up automated input systems for all four ingredients to maintain continuous production."
	]
	quest.5D114E6833D0AAF3.title: "Tuff + Glowstone Dust + Water + Moon Cobblestone → Moon Cobblestone"
	quest.5D19586551060173.quest_subtitle: "Used to connect electrical connectors."
	quest.5D23961C159EA3B6.title: "Obtain a &bTide Armour Trim&r"
	quest.5D37224940B99CF7.quest_desc: [
		"The Route Planner lets you create and modify train schedules."
		""
		"§7To plan a route:"
		"§71. Select a train from the Train List"
		"§72. Click 'Edit Schedule'"
		"§73. Add stations to visit in sequence"
		"§74. Configure wait times and conditions at each stop"
		"§75. Apply the schedule to your train"
		""
		"§7Tip: Use the 'Wait for' conditions to create smart automated trains that only depart when loaded/unloaded!"
	]
	quest.5D37224940B99CF7.title: "Route Planning"
	quest.5D38B2F83D218EE3.quest_subtitle: "Can pump long distances."
	quest.5D3BC15BB642B6A7.quest_desc: [
		"Before heading out on your archeological expedition, you'll need the right tools."
		""
		"The §bBrush§r is essential for carefully removing dirt and sand from suspicious blocks."
		""
		"The §bArcheology Hammer§r helps you collect fossils and artifacts without damaging them."
	]
	quest.5D3BC15BB642B6A7.title: "Essential Tools"
	quest.5D41EAE67770621C.quest_desc: [
		"Congratulations on completing the basics of Create!"
		"You now have the fundamental tools and knowledge to begin your engineering journey."
		""
		"§7Tip: The next chapter will introduce you to more advanced machinery and automation."
		""
		"§6Important: Make sure you have plenty of andesite alloy and iron sheets before moving forward!"
		""
		"§bClick the checkmark."
	]
	quest.5D41EAE67770621C.title: "Moving Forward"
	quest.5D516CF6207EB9D3.quest_desc: [
		"Create a musical composition by playing and recording a song!"
		""
		"§7Use your instrument and a music sheet to record a melody."
		""
		"§7Once recorded, you can play it back anywhere or share it with friends."
	]
	quest.5D516CF6207EB9D3.title: "Your First Composition"
	quest.5D62CFC34513C29E.quest_desc: [
		"The Cold Eye is found in Igloos."
		""
		"§7Search for Igloos in snowy biomes."
		"§7Check for a trapdoor inside some igloos - it leads to a hidden basement!"
		"§7The Eye may be in chests in either the main igloo or its basement."
		""
		"§6Pro Tip: §7Not all igloos have basements. Look for a rug that might be covering a trapdoor. You can also find it via "
		"{ \"text\": \"killing the yeti\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"320B728B064451F3\" } }"
		""
		"{image:block_factorys_bosses:item/spawn_egg/yeti_spawn_egg width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.5D6412CE78F5295A.quest_desc: [
		"§6Legacy Block Museum"
		""
		"Create a museum display of Minecraft's history!"
		""
		"§7Museum elements to include:"
		"§7• Displays of each legacy block"
		"§7• Information signs about each item"
		"§7• Timeline of Minecraft versions"
		"§7• Interactive elements"
		""
		"§6Pro Tip: §7Use item frames and signs to create educational displays"
	]
	quest.5D6412CE78F5295A.title: "§eLegacy Block Museum"
	quest.5D6C17A52F97153A.title: "Napalm Bomb"
	quest.5D78E59B68F31BED.quest_desc: [
		"Jupiter, the largest planet in our solar system, awaits your exploration!"
		""
		"To reach Jupiter, you'll need to build a Tier 5 Rocket using Juperium materials sourced from asteroids."
		""
		"Jupiter features:"
		"• High gravity (24.79)"
		"• No oxygen"
		"• Solar power rating: 11"
		"• Temperature: -126°C"
		"• Tier 4 planet"
		""
		"Prepare yourself for extreme conditions and unique resources!"
	]
	quest.5D78E59B68F31BED.title: "The Cosmic Gateway"
	quest.5D84A485688322A2.quest_desc: ["The &62x1 drawer&r holds &616 stacks&r in each of the option slots"]
	quest.5D84A485688322A2.quest_subtitle: "What it holds"
	quest.5DC04E936F35EE28.quest_desc: [
		"§7If you followed Chapter 2 correctly, you should already have iron nugget automation set up."
		""
		"§7Your existing automation system should be:"
		"§71. Converting cobblestone to gravel using a §fCrusher"
		"§72. §fWashing §7gravel using an §fEncased Fan §7with water to obtain iron nuggets"
		""
		"§7You can reuse this automation for Chapter 3's sealed mechanism production."
	]
	quest.5DC04E936F35EE28.title: "Already Automated: Iron Nuggets"
	quest.5DC78A44FC4F864A.quest_desc: [
		"§7Time to automate basic cutting board recipes!"
		""
		"§fSetup:§7"
		"§71. Place a §fSlicer§7 and power it with a §fCreate§7 source"
		"§72. Use §fbelts/funnels§7 to feed ingredients in"
		"§73. Collect processed ingredients with §fbelts/chutes§7"
		""
		"§7Processes any §fCutting Board§7 recipe that uses a knife automatically!"
		""
		"§7Try automating §fdough production§7 by slicing wheat into flour, then mixing with water in a basin!"
	]
	quest.5DC78A44FC4F864A.title: "Basic Ingredient Processing"
	quest.5DC9BE9A8D1C9B50.quest_desc: [
		"§7For the ultimate kitchen automation, let's build a fully integrated food storage system!"
		""
		"§fSetup:§7"
		"§71. Use §fstorage drawers/barrels§7 for raw ingredients"
		"§72. Store processed ingredients in §fcabinets§7 (keeps food fresh!)"
		"§73. Connect everything with §fCreate belts§7 and §ffunnels§7"
		"§74. Use §fmechanical arms§7 to move items between storage and machines"
		""
		"§fBonus:§7 Add §ffilters§7 to sort different food types automatically!"
	]
	quest.5DC9BE9A8D1C9B50.title: "Food Storage Automation"
	quest.5DE1DAE7AECE29FF.title: "Locate an &5End City&r"
	quest.5E04B024C8E9B865.quest_subtitle: "Used for filling items with fluids and crafting certain items using fluids."
	quest.5E1037F862E1B9B3.quest_desc: [
		"The Old Eye is found in Desert Pyramids."
		""
		"§7Search for Desert Pyramids in desert biomes."
		"§7Be careful of the TNT trap beneath the colored terracotta."
		"§7Check all the chests thoroughly."
		""
		"§6Pro Tip: §7Or you can kill the sandworm via the sandworm quest to get the eye."
		"{image:block_factorys_bosses:item/spawn_egg/sandworm_spawn_egg width:100 height:100 align:center}"
		""
		"{ \"text\": \"Quest\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"661D553B47E15C4E\" } }"
	]
	quest.5E1A35C47F347B0C.quest_subtitle: "Collect beetroot and a beetroot seed"
	quest.5E44A66399181394.quest_desc: ["§7Using §fMechanical Crafter§7, combine §fZinc Nuggets§7 with §fInfernal Mechanisms§7 and §fAndesite Alloys§7 to create §fEngine Pistons§7."]
	quest.5E44A66399181394.title: "Zinc Nugget + Infernal Mechanism + Andesite Alloy -> Engine Piston"
	quest.5E6604B5EFF3CE2C.quest_desc: [
		"§7The terrain of The Otherside is as unique as it is dangerous:"
		""
		"§6Notable features:"
		"§7• Sculk Stone - the foundation of this realm"
		"§7• Echo Soil - vibrating earth that amplifies sounds"
		"§7• Blooming Sculk - flora adapted to the sculk ecosystem"
		"§7• Sculk Tendrils - reaching growths that sense movement"
		"§7• Sculk Grime - viscous substance with unique properties"
		""
		"§6Exploration tactics:"
		"§7• Build elevated pathways to avoid ground-dwelling threats"
		"§7• Mark your paths to prevent getting lost"
		"§7• Establish waypoints with recognizable landmarks"
		"§7• Listen carefully - sound cues often warn of danger"
		""
		"§cWarning: §7The laws of physics and nature seem altered in this realm. Familiar potions and effects may behave unpredictably."
	]
	quest.5E6604B5EFF3CE2C.title: "Alien Landscape"
	quest.5E66F5E97B0DF20D.quest_desc: [
		"The Redwood Thicket features massive redwood trees that tower into the sky."
		""
		"§6Features:"
		"§7• Giant redwood trees"
		"§7• Unique wood type"
		"§7• Dense forest canopy"
		""
		"These massive trees provide large amounts of wood and make for impressive building sites."
	]
	quest.5E66F5E97B0DF20D.title: "Land of Giants"
	quest.5E70064753A3D30D.quest_desc: [
		"Using the desh obtained from the Moon, you can now craft your Tier 2 Rocket! This more advanced spacecraft will allow you to reach Mars."
		""
		"The Red Planet awaits with new resources and challenges!"
		""
		"§7Tip: Mars has more hostile conditions than the Moon, so prepare accordingly."
	]
	quest.5E70064753A3D30D.title: "Mars Awaits!"
	quest.5E71D2CF0EB03471.quest_desc: [
		"§7The §fCasualness Delight§7 mod brings relaxing, everyday meals to your automation lineup!"
		""
		"§7These comfortable dishes are perfect for casual days and provide consistent benefits."
		""
		"§fSetup:§7"
		"§71. Create farms for everyday ingredients using §fsprinklers§7"
		"§72. Process ingredients casually with §fslicers§7 and §fmixers§7"
		"§73. Set up §fcooking pots§7 for the final casual cooking"
		"§74. Use §fdeployers§7 to assemble the finished casual meals"
		""
		"§fTIP:§7 Casual meals might seem simple, but their automation can be incredibly efficient!"
	]
	quest.5E71D2CF0EB03471.title: "Casual Cooking Automation"
	quest.5E74431A2653E193.quest_desc: [
		"The Create mod revolves around rotational power. The hand crank is your first way to generate this power."
		""
		"§7Simply place it on a mechanical block and right-click to turn it manually."
		""
		"§7While this is fine for testing, you'll want more sustainable power sources soon."
	]
	quest.5E74431A2653E193.title: "Manual Labor"
	quest.5E783474BA6980E3.quest_subtitle: "You can craft while you're away from your main base, but remember that it is quite costly for such a benefit."
	quest.5E996B8F0BEF8D75.quest_desc: [
		"§7The Shattered are twisted entities that roam the Otherside, remnants of something once human but now corrupted beyond recognition."
		""
		"§7These dangerous creatures:"
		"§7• Move erratically with unnatural speed"
		"§7• Can teleport short distances when threatened"
		"§7• Emit disorienting sounds that mask their approach"
		"§7• Strike with devastating force"
		""
		"§7When defeated, they may drop valuable items including:"
		"§7• §fEcho Shards§7"
		"§7• Rare sculk-infused materials"
		"§7• Occasionally, unique artifacts of unknown origin"
		""
		"§7Study their behavior patterns and movement to develop effective combat strategies. Their unpredictable nature makes them one of the most dangerous threats in this dimension."
	]
	quest.5E996B8F0BEF8D75.title: "Twisted Remnants"
	quest.5E9BC860650BC3C6.quest_desc: [
		"Aquaculture 2 A fishing expansion that adds over 30 new fish species across biomes, along with new rods, bait, and loot. Now oceans, rivers, and even the Nether’s lava lakes (with the right equipment) teem with life to catch. You can craft an Iron or Gold Fishing Rod, use bait like worms or minnows, and reel in everything from trout to turtles (and treasure). Aquaculture makes fishing a viable source of food and rare resources – some fish can be cooked into special meals or used alchemically. It’s a peaceful but engaging counterpart to the pack’s combat, perfect for when you want a calmer gameplay moment that still progresses your survival."
		""
		"Fishing Overhaul Enhances the fishing mechanic with a skill-based mini-game. When a fish bites, you’ll need to keep a moving cursor within a green zone to reel it in, reminiscent of Stardew Valley’s fishing system. A critical catch (perfect timing in the small sweet spot) can even yield extra loot. This mod works with Aquaculture’s content, meaning all the new fish can be caught through the engaging new system. Fishing becomes more interactive and rewarding, turning it into a fun diversion that can still net you valuable items (or just dinner)."
	]
	quest.5EB59B43781EB61D.quest_desc: [
		"Wrench it to switch input/output."
		""
		"Input is marked with a &3blue&r connection and output is marked with an &6orange&r "
		"connection."
		""
		"When converting FE to TFMG energy, the desired voltage can be set up to 250V."
	]
	quest.5EB59B43781EB61D.quest_subtitle: "Converts TFMG energy to FE and back."
	quest.5F1C371B9CF45003.quest_subtitle: "Fill up your backpack from your storage"
	quest.5F1E7D3B9A8C2E6D.quest_desc: [
		"Sharestones are specialized waystones that can only connect to other sharestones of the same color."
		""
		"Create a Sharestone using sequenced assembly with crying obsidian as the base, along with a Warp Stone and Create's Linked Controller."
		""
		"Perfect for creating private teleportation networks!"
	]
	quest.5F1E7D3B9A8C2E6D.title: "Private Network Teleporter"
	quest.5F54692C554A45BE.quest_subtitle: "Use on a Diesel Engine to silence it. Create Diesel Generators"
	quest.5F630ED2E1FA4705.quest_desc: ["Maybe useful for Valkerian Skies / Trackworks vehicles?"]
	quest.5F630ED2E1FA4705.quest_subtitle: "Manually control the speed of your engine."
	quest.5F68F1D8533B534F.quest_desc: ["Right click on the industrial mixer to install it."]
	quest.5F68F1D8533B534F.quest_subtitle: "Sorry, I have to stir this pot every five minutes."
	quest.5F8F8BB3BF640A17.title: "Locate a &eDesert Pyramid&r"
	quest.5F98083A1EF33FD9.quest_desc: [
		"§6Diamond Tier Storage"
		""
		"Premium storage solution!"
		""
		"§7Features:"
		"§7• Base: 27 slots"
		"§7• Upgrade: +36 slots"
		"§7• Total: 63 slots"
		""
		"§6Additional Benefits:"
		"§7• 4 upgrade slots"
		"§7• Maximum protection"
		"§7• Fastest access speed"
	]
	quest.5F98083A1EF33FD9.title: "§eDiamond Storage Tier"
	quest.5FB93D510397F58F.quest_desc: [
		"§7Raw oil is useless for powering rockets - it must be processed into rocket-grade fuel. The §fFuel Refinery§7 performs this crucial conversion."
		""
		"§7This advanced processing unit:"
		"§7• Cracks long hydrocarbon chains into more volatile compounds"
		"§7• Removes impurities that could damage engine components"
		"§7• Adds stabilizers to prevent premature combustion"
		"§7• Outputs refined fuel ready for spacecraft consumption"
		""
		"§7Create an automated pipeline from your oil collection through the refinery to fuel storage tanks. The journey to the stars requires significant fuel reserves, so efficiency in this process is paramount."
		""
		"§7Without proper refinement, your rocket engines would fail catastrophically during the extreme stress of liftoff."
	]
	quest.5FB93D510397F58F.title: "Liquid Propulsion"
	quest.5FD9B6DE2773C89E.quest_desc: [
		"Ancient §bTotems§r were used by ancient civilizations for protection and blessings."
		""
		"Search for totem fragments in ruins and piece them together to create powerful totems:"
		""
		"- §bTotem of Radiance§r - Damages hostile mobs and makes them glow"
		"- §bTotem of Torrent§r - Provides speed boost when used"
		"- §bTotem of Growth§r - Accelerates crop growth in the surrounding area"
	]
	quest.5FD9B6DE2773C89E.title: "Ancient Totems"
	quest.5FF4D92A9D052F44.quest_desc: [
		"§7The Otherside offers unique equipment that harnesses the power of sculk:"
		""
		"§6Warden Armor:"
		"§7• Extremely durable protection"
		"§7• Provides enhanced vision in darkness"
		"§7• Reduces the detection range of sculk sensors"
		""
		"§6Warden Sword:"
		"§7• Deals significant damage"
		"§7• Has a chance to inflict a blindness effect"
		"§7• More effective against non-sculk creatures"
		""
		"§6Soul Elytra:"
		"§7• Enhanced version of the standard Elytra"
		"§7• Allows for faster and more controlled flight"
		"§7• Has a special boost ability"
		""
		"§6Sonorous Staff:"
		"§7• Channels the sonic power of the Warden"
		"§7• Creates devastating sonic booms"
		"§7• Effective crowd control weapon"
	]
	quest.5FF4D92A9D052F44.title: "Mastering the Sculk"
	quest.5FF617620A38A716.quest_subtitle: "As the name implies this item allows you to glue blocks together. Perticularly useful when making contraptions. Good thing we don't have fingers or the glue will stick to our hands... wait."
	quest.5FF65A2F5BFBE6D7.quest_desc: [
		"Advanced Display Blocks from Railways Navigator provide real-time information about your trains and network."
		""
		"§7You can use these display blocks to:"
		"§71. Show train arrival/departure times at stations"
		"§72. Display current train locations and status"
		"§73. Create automated announcement boards"
		""
		"§7Connect these displays to your Navigator system and place them at stations or control centers for a professional railway management system!"
	]
	quest.5FF65A2F5BFBE6D7.title: "Advanced Train Displays"
	quest.5FF9AD0A23CA1A86.title: "Obtain Vanadium Block"
	quest.604BD106B78DF013.quest_desc: [
		"§7Set up a §fLava Production System§7 using §fDripstone and Cauldrons§7 or an §fIgneous Extruder§7."
		""
		"§7Use §fFluid Pipes§7 with §fEncased Fans§7 to cool the system and prevent overheating."
	]
	quest.604BD106B78DF013.title: "Lava Production"
	quest.6056B16BA2D3CA69.quest_desc: [
		"§7If you followed Chapter 2 correctly, you should already have cobblestone automation set up."
		""
		"§7Your existing automation system should be using one of these methods:"
		"§71. A §fMechanical Generator §7for lag-free cobblestone production"
		"§72. A cobblestone farm using lava and water with §fMechanical Drills §7or §fBlock Breakers"
		""
		"§7You'll need a steady supply of cobblestone for many recipes in this chapter!"
	]
	quest.6056B16BA2D3CA69.title: "Already Automated: Cobblestone"
	quest.607FE56A60D6233E.quest_subtitle: "Save hotbar slots, only have the tool for the job out. Left click the block to tell it what you want to interact with"
	quest.608A74EE3C04347E.quest_desc: ["The &6spout&r can be used to drop liquid onto an item that's below it on a depot or belt to be able to change what the item is"]
	quest.608A74EE3C04347E.quest_subtitle: "Liquid used in crafting?"
	quest.6096FD990F399727.quest_desc: [
		"§7There are mutliple methods to automate cobblestone using Create. "
		""
		"§7But what I reccomend is using the §fMechanical Generator§7, since it reduces lag by not mining a physical block. "
		""
		"§7The §fMechanical Generator §7is also very fast. "
	]
	quest.6096FD990F399727.title: "Cobblestone"
	quest.609FC1AA946FCE5A.quest_subtitle: "Make an axe"
	quest.609FC1AA946FCE5A.title: "Becoming a lumberjack"
	quest.60C91DB4E99253B8.title: "Obtain Limesand"
	quest.60C98BB1CDD7968B.quest_desc: [
		"§7Lumiere is the second type of crystal found in Crystal Canyons."
		""
		"§7These dazzling pink crystals emit a warm glow and are perfect for crafting decorative items and light sources."
		""
		"§7Harvest them with care to collect lumiere shards for your crafting needs."
		""
		"§7The gentle light from these crystals can be used to create beautiful atmospheric lighting in your builds."
	]
	quest.60C98BB1CDD7968B.title: "Pink Crystal Treasures"
	quest.60D073A200595414.quest_subtitle: "Lets you see the current stress and stress capacity of a kinetic network, not the stress of someone else."
	quest.60D16B35E11D9F7F.quest_desc: ["Iris is installed to allow for enabling of shaders. "]
	quest.60D16B35E11D9F7F.title: "Shaders Available"
	quest.616D6F2701F7EE81.quest_desc: ["FindMe allows you to search for items in nearby inventories by pressing a key. For that you simply need to hover over an item (JEI Compatible) and press \"Y\" (By default) and cloud particles will spawn in the inventories that have that item."]
	quest.616D6F2701F7EE81.title: "FindMe"
	quest.6177966365A058A2.quest_desc: [
		"&3Steel vats&r required in a 2x2x2 box, plus heated."
		""
		"Either copper or zinc electrodes will work. Make sure to pump out the CO2."
		""
		"The electrode holders require a minimum of &25A&r to work, meaning they must be supplied with at least &3500V&r each. This can be achieved with one max speed &6generator&r and a &6transformer&r with a turn ratio of &e4.&r"
	]
	quest.6177966365A058A2.quest_subtitle: "How to make aluminum."
	quest.6177966365A058A2.title: "Aluminum Electrolysis"
	quest.617D59D4F14FA3AE.quest_subtitle: "Allows for contraptions that traverse rails in the same way minecarts do."
	quest.618FF4D4A0FCC14C.quest_subtitle: "Lets you place down a mirror that assists you in building symmetrical things."
	quest.61B3B50BE9D0A6E5.quest_subtitle: "Reduces the total stack size to 1 stack "
	quest.61BCE8506F68DB58.quest_desc: [
		"§7Lumiere clusters are beautiful crystalline formations that emit a soft, pink glow."
		""
		"§7These decorative blocks can be used to light up your base with a warm, inviting ambiance."
		""
		"§7Try placing them on walls or ceilings for a magical effect!"
		""
		"§7Grow your own clusters using a Lumiere Compounder - it slowly turns Lumiere Shards into full clusters."
	]
	quest.61BCE8506F68DB58.title: "Luminous Clusters"
	quest.61C12A798AA01EBB.quest_desc: [
		"The §bOcelot Fossil§r is a prized find that keeps creepers at a distance."
		""
		"When placed or held, creepers within a 20-block radius will avoid you."
		""
		"This makes it invaluable for exploration, especially in dark caves."
	]
	quest.61D6F7DB6E8B68DC.title: "Use an Helve Hammer to process materials"
	quest.61E314CCB5583825.quest_desc: [
		"§6ME Terminal"
		""
		"Your network interface!"
		""
		"§7Terminal Types:"
		"§7• ME Terminal (Items)"
		"§7• Fluid Terminal"
		"§7• Pattern Terminal"
		"§7• Interface Terminal"
		""
		"§6Features:"
		"§7• Search functions"
		"§7• Sort options"
		"§7• Quick transfer"
		""
		"§6Pro Tip: §7Learn terminal shortcuts!"
	]
	quest.61E314CCB5583825.title: "§eNetwork Access"
	quest.6228DF70D61D7EAC.quest_desc: [
		"§7Direct a portion of your automated §fTuff§7 production to your Moon Cobblestone creation process."
		""
		"§7This durable stone provides the foundation for the lunar material."
		""
		"§7Ensure proper ratios with other ingredients for optimal production efficiency."
	]
	quest.6228DF70D61D7EAC.title: "Tuff"
	quest.62316183AAFBD68B.quest_subtitle: "Mixing Thorium, Stone and Clay in water will generate thorium"
	quest.62316183AAFBD68B.title: "Generating thorium"
	quest.6239924D434EC029.quest_desc: [
		"§7If you followed the questline correctly in Chapter 3: Industrial Revolution, you should already have iron ingot automation set up."
		""
		"§7If not, refer back to those quests to establish a reliable iron supply."
	]
	quest.6239924D434EC029.title: "Already Automated: Iron Ingots"
	quest.623C08C1038D7038.quest_desc: ["§7To create §fZinc Sheets§7, you'll need to process zinc ingots through a §fMechanical Press§7."]
	quest.623C08C1038D7038.title: "Zinc Ingot -> Zinc Sheet"
	quest.62A5DAB07FB1A365.quest_desc: ["The Meshtrap block is tailored for static setups, perfect for underwater fishery hubs. When placed, it captures fish entities it encounters and gathers nearby items. Unlike the Frametrap, it operates only in a stationary state, seamlessly integrating with your logistics system to transport collected resources for processing. Ideal for creating efficient, automated fishery operations."]
	quest.62A5DAB07FB1A365.quest_subtitle: "Read Desc"
	quest.62A5DE7E34113E9D.quest_desc: [
		"Villages are excellent places to start your journey."
		"They offer shelter, resources, and trading opportunities with villagers."
		"Find one to establish your first base of operations!"
		""
		"§7Tip: Look for village structures in plains, deserts, or snowy biomes."
		""
		"§7Tip: Villagers can offer valuable trades that will help you progress through your adventure."
	]
	quest.62AC675062FBF45C.quest_desc: ["Display mod is installed. "]
	quest.62D4F42CE66EB5DF.quest_desc: [
		"§d§lWelcome to Create: Cogs and Cataclysm!"
		""
		"&7Immerse yourself in Create: Cogs and Cataclysm, a modpack where mechanical ingenuity meets high-stakes adventure. Built around the Create mod’s extensive automation and L_Ender’s Cataclysm's impressive dungeons and boss battles. This pack invites you to engineer contraptions that reshape the world while braving perilous expeditions across enhanced Overworld, Nether, and End realms. You’ll devise complex factories of gears and steam, then deploy your inventions to conquer dungeons and boss lairs teeming with mutant creatures and legendary foes. The world is richly transformed – towering biomes and ancient structures beg to be explored, and each dimension holds new challenges. From the Overworld’s lush Terralith vistas and sprawling Tectonic mountains to the Nether’s Incendium-scorched wastes and the End’s surreal Nullscape spires, you’ll experience Minecraft at its most awe-inspiring. Yet these beautiful landscapes are fraught with danger: deadly bosses lie in wait, and nights can bring blood moons and mutant sieges.&r"
		""
		"&7Through it all, Create’s mechanical prowess serves as your edge. Build automated farms to sustain you through survival challenges like Spice of Life’s Carrot's dietary benefits, and weaponize yourself in battle. Combat itself is reinvented: enhanced movement and weaponry mods let you duel with fluid Better Combat combos and perform acrobatic dodge rolls, making every fight dynamic and exciting. Gear progression is equally deep, with artifacts and relics granting abilities that may turn the tide of difficult encounters. Create: Cogs and Cataclysm strikes a careful balance between automation and exploration – you must be as skilled at designing contraptions and supply lines as you are at delving into dark catacombs or facing colossal bosses. The adventures span the breadth of Minecraft’s lore: archaeological digs for lost artifacts, epic boss battles that require strategy and grit, and expeditions through uncharted biomes with only your wits and machines to protect you. Prepare to unleash your inner engineer-adventurer with confidence – the world of Create: Cogs and Cataclysm awaits, full of mechanical marvels and mythic challenges at every turn.&r"
		""
		"§d§lKey Features:"
		"§7✦ Create Mod's comprehensive automation system"
		"§7✦ Cataclysm's Elden Ring style boss fights"
		"§7✦ Relic and Artifacts' unique abilities and power"
		"§7✦ Farmer's Delight's deep cooking mechanics"
		"§7✦ Enhanced building with Chipped and more"
		"§7✦ Dynamic terrain generation with enhanced biomes"
		"§7✦ Custom advancements and challenges"
		""
		"§6Modpack Philosophy:"
		"§7This pack was designed to provide a balanced experience that rewards creativity and exploration. Whether you're a technical builder, an adventurer, or a decorator, you'll find something to enjoy in Create: Cogs and Cataclysm."
		""
		"§6Are you ready to begin your journey?"
	]
	quest.62D4F42CE66EB5DF.title: "§d§lYour Adventure Begins"
	quest.62DE24AD061AC90F.title: "Visit a &dNether Fortress&r"
	quest.6307E7CBD7C5B062.quest_desc: ["Use a &emechanical press&r with either a basin or a depot."]
	quest.6307E7CBD7C5B062.quest_subtitle: "Pleather. Presstoff. Whatever hard-to-pronouce name you wanna call it."
	quest.631BFADC22A27777.quest_desc: [
		"A Minecraft mod to solve the long-standing issue of not looking cool enough."
		"Transmog allows you to change the appearance of items without modifying their behavior at all!"
		"It works on armor, weapons, tools and anything else you can imagine!"
	]
	quest.631BFADC22A27777.quest_subtitle: "Think WoW Transmog"
	quest.6356507E1CF1E4C1.quest_desc: ["§7Smelt certus quartz dust, preferrably using a encased fan and lava. "]
	quest.6356507E1CF1E4C1.title: "Certus Quartz Dust -> Silicon"
	quest.6358A145E9CDFDDA.quest_desc: [
		"The &6draw controller&r is the main item you will want to use to automatically put your items into drawers that are linked to the controller."
		""
		"It has a range of 12 blocks from each side, a &625x25x25&r cube with the controller as the middle block."
	]
	quest.6358A145E9CDFDDA.quest_subtitle: "The brains of storage drawers"
	quest.63F4830C04865359.title: "Change Belt Grinder skin via right-click with an Sand Paper"
	quest.63F8B6B7A98156E6.quest_desc: [
		"§6Wireless Access"
		""
		"Remote network control!"
		""
		"§7Components Needed:"
		"§7• Wireless Access Point"
		"§7• Security Terminal"
		"§7• Wireless Terminal"
		""
		"§6Features:"
		"§7• Remote access"
		"§7• Security settings"
		"§7• Range boosters"
		""
		"§6Pro Tip: §7Use quantum link for infinite range!"
	]
	quest.63F8B6B7A98156E6.title: "§eWireless Network"
	quest.642172D58E8B11E1.quest_subtitle: "A kinetic source that uses the flow of water as its source of energy. Will generate the same amount of SU at the same RPM as long as one block of flowing water is adjacent.\\n\\nYou can also swich the look of your water wheel by right-clicking it with pretty much any wood plank (including ones from other mods)."
	quest.6424E217477EA9CD.quest_desc: [
		"Night is approaching and you'll need a place to rest. Craft a sleeping bag to safely pass the night without setting your spawn point."
		""
		"§7Tip: Sleeping bags are portable and won't reset your spawn point like beds do."
		""
		"§7Tip: You can craft them using wool and any wooden planks."
		""
		"§7Warning: Monsters still spawn at night, so make sure you're in a safe spot!"
	]
	quest.6424E217477EA9CD.title: "A Good Night's Rest"
	quest.64341D7F6E892900.quest_subtitle: "Disenchant item and collect experience as liquid."
	quest.64407A1BC7A1761B.quest_subtitle: "Start of the exp journey"
	quest.645DDBD12EC8DF82.quest_desc: ["Frostmaws are dangerous beasts found rarely in snowy areas. Their massive size, impressive speed, and powerful ice breath make them near-impossible opponents. If, on your travels, you encounter one sleeping in your path, it's likely best to take a different route and let it lay. The beast guards a precious ice crystal that can unleash pure winter energy when wielded."]
	quest.648C13279144617F.title: "Better solar"
	quest.64C1537889D9485F.quest_desc: [
		"§6The Tinkering Table"
		""
		"The Tinkering Table is your ultimate tool for working with redstone components and mechanical items."
		""
		"§7Materials you can work with:"
		"§7• Redstone blocks and components"
		"§7• Mechanical devices"
		"§7• Lanterns and light sources"
		"§7• Metal components and fixtures"
		""
		"§6Pro Tip: §7Use variant redstone lamps and lanterns to create ambiance with functional lighting."
	]
	quest.64C1537889D9485F.title: "Mechanical Marvels"
	quest.64CC214BD1AA5791.quest_subtitle: "Make some Copper Armor"
	quest.64CC214BD1AA5791.title: "Starter Armor"
	quest.6553CDC45C522E7F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6mixer&r has many different recipes that it can be used for."
		""
		"One of the recipes is it can make &6andesite alloy&r in a more efficient manner only costing 1 andesite and 1 iron/zinc nugget"
	]
	quest.6553CDC45C522E7F.quest_subtitle: "It's got a lot of uses"
	quest.6553CDC45C522E7F.title: "Mechanical Mixer and Basin"
	quest.657FE1419444750E.title: "Locate &5The Stronghold&r"
	quest.65A2AC554D856D93.quest_subtitle: "Allows for contraptions that move across gantries."
	quest.65A7B594A51E3C98.quest_desc: [
		"§6Enhanced Dungeons"
		""
		"Vanilla dungeons have been completely redesigned to be more exciting and challenging."
		""
		"§7Enhanced dungeon features:"
		"§7• Larger, more complex layouts"
		"§7• Better treasure and loot variety"
		"§7• Unique puzzles and traps"
		"§7• Themed rooms and areas"
		""
		"§6Pro Tip: §7Look for hidden wall sections and false floors - many dungeons now contain secret areas with special treasures."
	]
	quest.65A7B594A51E3C98.title: "Dungeon Depths"
	quest.65A90A762D0D3F38.quest_desc: ["§7To create §fPrinted Silicon§7, you'll need to use §fDeployers§7 with the §fInscriber Silicon Press§7 on silicon."]
	quest.65A90A762D0D3F38.title: "Silicon -> Printed Silicon"
	quest.65EA25D2DDEE694F.quest_subtitle: "Slow but easy to maneuver. Immersive Aircraft"
	quest.65EC813AEB11FE54.quest_desc: [
		"Your Tier 1 Rocket is your first step to the stars! With it, you can reach Earth's orbit and the Moon."
		""
		"Make sure to bring:"
		"- Space Suit (for oxygen)"
		"- Oxygen tanks"
		"- Fuel"
		"- Basic supplies like food"
		""
		"§7Tip: Place your launch pad with clear space above it and fuel your rocket before launching."
	]
	quest.65EC813AEB11FE54.title: "To the Moon!"
	quest.65FD004534739EC2.quest_subtitle: "The backpack will last forever"
	quest.661D553B47E15C4E.quest_desc: ["The Sandworm is buried beneath the desert sands and surfaces with a violent strike, swallowing blocks and mobs. It can burrow and ambush, making it an unpredictable threat. Sandworm Nest Structure"]
	quest.666E9828756ADB0C.quest_subtitle: "The basis of most things fluid related in Create.\\n\\nCan also be used to encase fluid pipes."
	quest.6670C6A95D9E11FE.quest_desc: ["Also adds Stat Frame. Works very similar to an Advancement Frame"]
	quest.669FDF2411FD57AA.quest_desc: [
		"The functioning is very simple, 8 new Ender chests have been incorporated, each one consisting of a mineral, and adding the following additional space slots."
		""
		"Iron (+1 row)"
		"Copper (+1 row)"
		"Gold (+2 row)"
		"Lapis Lazuli (+2 row)"
		"Redstone (+2 row)"
		"Diamond (+3 rows)"
		"Emerald (+4 rows)"
		"Netherite (+5 rows)"
		""
		"To get the Ender Iron or Copper chests, you will need an Ender chest and surround it with the same mineral. The same with the rest of the chests, for example, to get the Ender Gold chest, you will need a copper or iron Ender chest, and surround it with gold."
	]
	quest.66A35D1A11CBB671.quest_subtitle: "Assemble a Control Chip"
	quest.66A35D1A11CBB671.title: "Precision Fabrication"
	quest.66CB492E7998E6B8.quest_desc: [
		"Ribbits will add swamp villages full of tiny frog villagers called ribbits!"
		"These little guys will sometimes sit down in groups to play music, which you can join in with!"
		""
		" Merchant and fisherman ribbits can be traded with for various items including the new ribbits plant blocks and maracas!"
		"Sorcerer ribbits will occasionally cast spells to buff the player, and all gardener ribbits will water crops! "
		""
		"Ribbits will naturally return to their homes at night, but if you'd like to relocate them, you can reset their home point to their current position by right clicking them with amethyst. "
		"{image:ribbits:item/toadstool width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.66EB092315C08AAA.quest_subtitle: "Press &c\"Z\"&r To see How to Build It"
	quest.66EB092315C08AAA.title: "AHAHAH Pollution, who cares"
	quest.67148DE49E107A59.quest_desc: [
		"§7Congratulations! You've successfully automated the production of §fSpace Grade Alloy§7 - the cornerstone material for all your space adventures."
		""
		"§7This special alloy will be used to craft §frocket parts§7, §fspace stations§7, and advanced equipment needed for lunar exploration."
		""
		"§7With this automation complete, you're one step closer to launching your first rocket to the moon!"
	]
	quest.67148DE49E107A59.title: "Molten Space Grade Alloy → Space Grade Alloy"
	quest.672C61B048CB3B85.quest_subtitle: "In order to make a train you're going to need at least:\\n- 1 Train Casing\\n- 1 Train Station\\n- Enough train tracks to make your railroad.\\n\\nIn order to see how you assemble a train \"ponder\" the train station."
	quest.677179FC764889AB.quest_desc: [
		"Pipe crude oil into the &6distillation controller&r and take products from each of the outputs. "
		""
		"Blaze burner heating is required. The steel tanks can be 1x1, 2x2, or 3x3, with larger sizes accomodating more heating which can increase distilling rate."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The minimum height tower has three outputs and makes &0Heavy oil&r, &6Diesel&r, and &eGasoline&r"
		""
		"Add two more outputs and you can make &7LPG&r and &9Kerosene&r"
		""
		"One more output lets you extract &4Naphtha&r"
		""
		"Outputs can be set to void excess fluid or stop refining when full to prevent wasting oil."
	]
	quest.677179FC764889AB.quest_subtitle: "Build a distillation tower."
	quest.677179FC764889AB.title: "Distillery District"
	quest.678996586F76CDEF.quest_desc: [
		"§6Pickup Upgrade"
		""
		"Automatic item collection!"
		""
		"§7Features:"
		"§7• Auto-pickup items"
		"§7• Filter support"
		"§7• Range control"
		""
		"§6Advanced Options:"
		"§7• Whitelist/Blacklist"
		"§7• NBT matching"
		"§7• Damage matching"
		""
		"§6Pro Tip: §7Great for mining automation!"
	]
	quest.678996586F76CDEF.title: "§ePickup Upgrade"
	quest.67B3D0A82F1BB3EA.quest_subtitle: "The basis for more advanced blocks."
	quest.67CE399D0A9C0F57.quest_subtitle: "Blocks that both allow for automatic crafting of normal recipes and the crafting of recipes that are bigger than a normal crafting table would allow for."
	quest.67F7FBDD9CC782F7.quest_desc: [
		"There are three tiers of vats:"
		""
		"1. &8Cast iron&r"
		"2. &3Steel&r"
		"3. &4Fireproof&r"
		""
		"Different recipes may only work with a certain tier or better."
		""
		"&6Mixer&r and &6centrifuge&r recipes only need one vat block to work."
		"&dElectrolyzer&r or &darc furnace&r recipes need larger vats and the minimum LxWxH dimensions will be called out where necessary."
		""
		"Some recipes will require &6heating.&r One normal &6blaze burner&r is not enough; you will either need more than one or have to &bsuperheat&r it. &cFireboxes&r act like superheated blaze burners."
		""
		"You can wrench them to see inside!"
	]
	quest.67F7FBDD9CC782F7.quest_subtitle: "I have no idea vat I'm doing."
	quest.67F7FBDD9CC782F7.title: "Chemical Vats"
